From a13b8b009efdde96af40661c34a0d9299b13b5bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:45:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 110/122] SPLINE: the R2013+ spline flags and knot parameter
 also from DXF

DXF has no splineflags and knotparam, so they were 0 from DXF, and
ACadSharp read the control point SPLINEs of DXFs written as R2013+ as
fit point splines and lost them (32 of the corpus). Set them as from
earlier DWGs, unless set otherwise.

* src/dwg.spec (SPLINE): Also from DXF with knotparam 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dwg.spec | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/dwg.spec b/src/dwg.spec
index 178046f..9dd06bc 100644
--- a/src/dwg.spec
+++ b/src/dwg.spec
@@ -2655,7 +2655,10 @@ DWG_ENTITY (SPLINE)
       // as AutoCAD: control points with a custom knot parameter, fit
       // points with method fit points and use knot parameter (chord).
       // ACadSharp takes the scenario from these.
-      if (dat->from_version < R_2013b && !(dwg->opts & DWG_OPTS_IN))
+      // DXF has them not: from DXF, unless set otherwise
+      if ((dat->from_version < R_2013b && !(dwg->opts & DWG_OPTS_IN))
+          || ((dwg->opts & DWG_OPTS_INDXF) && !FIELD_VALUE (knotparam)
+              && !(FIELD_VALUE (splineflags) & ~9)))
         {
           if (FIELD_VALUE (scenario) == 2)
             {
